  "summary": "Bounded revision of out/e2-results-review-20261003/e2_audit_aggregate.proposed.py only. No data, frozen analyzer, or hardware touched; no test was executed here, only proposed edits and the commands to verify them. Changes: (1) row provenance now reads the frozen workload from case[\"base\"] first (a_transfers never exists at the case top level), fixing 'input-a-transfers failed', 'raw-a-issue-count X vs None' and 'raw-a-done-count X vs None'; (2) a new read-only board audit walks runs/<id>/board, checks board/record.json == runs/<id>/record.json by sha256, exit.txt==0, taint.before/after==0, uname.before/after equality plus kernel_release containment, argv.txt vs plan argv and metadata argv, stderr presence, computes dmesg.before/after multiset difference as per-case new WARNING lines (never claims 'no warning' from taint 0), and verifies record.sha256 / archive.sha256 first sha token against the record, metadata and the hash of the archive; (3) archive.tar.gz is located in board/ or the run dir, hashed only with --hash-archives, and its members are hashed with tarfile.extractfile (read-only, nothing extracted) and compared against the local board files, with every mismatch going into problems; (4) fail-closed fixes: build_summary's bad set now includes rows with any problem, a legacy replay exception is a problem instead of only an error field, --legacy-analyzer import failure is a recorded global problem instead of a silent pass, a missing archive or missing/unreadable sha256 note is a failure, and main() exits 1 whenever any case is unclean or a global problem is open; (5) new raw evidence columns for 0x014/0x018 probe times and the 0x015/0x019 hit/self/other decode; (6) W/N A-context coverage from the legacy A-phase (phase==2) union of new ordinary valid entries, attributed with mapping[2] (A src) and mapping[3] (A dst) — mapping[0:2] is V, mapping[2:4] is A — with the deadline snapshot explicitly NOT used; (7) per-condition classification_counts, src/dst first-probe hit counts and A_removal_event counts in the summary, with short/boundary/prefix still counted separately because the group key stays phase/condition; (8) a new board-audit.json carrying full per-case board detail plus the complete legacy evidence. No hardcoded expected D88/D89/D8B-D8D values, no claim about warm 2-valid or flush_s1, and no 'invalid old tag implies not flushed' check were added; the earlier prefix-worker readings are treated as unverified and are not encoded.",
